\subsection{Overall Performance Assessment}
In summary, Evo performs better than other traditional machine learning techniques and the baseline model. The most remarkable performance is observed in battery degradation, which reduces by 36.36\%. This is a clear indicator of increased battery life. Moreover, Evo exhibits increased battery capacity retention at 93.4\%, an efficient charging mechanism at 0.944, and reduces thermal stress to 0.27.
In conclusion, it can be said that by including optimization techniques in machine learning algorithms, battery management for electric vehicles can be greatly improved. A more efficient approach can be seen in terms of battery longevity as well as overall performance.

