\section{CONCLUSION AND FUTURE WORK}
The paper focuses on a machine learning-based approach for smarter energy management systems and batteries for electric vehicles with a long lifespan. The experiments indicate that Evo outperforms all other machine learning algorithms in achieving a better result for battery lifespan. Evo provides the lowest level of degradation, or 36.36\% below the baseline model, while increasing battery capacity retention to 93.4\%, improving charging efficiency, and decreasing thermal stress by 35.71\%. In other words, Evo provides a more efficient lifespan for the battery in an EV in terms of control, efficiency, and resistance to degradation.

The research results indicate how optimized machine learning can be used for enhancing battery lifespan in EVs. By enhancing battery lifespan in EVs, batteries can be used for a longer lifespan while increasing driving range and making batteries more durable.

Future research can be conducted in several ways by including real-time data on how the car is used, how the environment is changing, and how electrical demands are changing in the near future. The model can be tested in real-life battery management systems.


